KG42.register("rules-acead20c6ed59633a0fe56e4",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R003","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Each prosumer submits its chosen next-slot energy-consumption quantity x_n^o to the MGO. Scope: Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot. The MGO is obligated to pursue maximization of its own profit when coordinating PV energy sharing. Scope: The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement. The MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance supplies and demands. Scope: The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM. Condition: An internal mismatch occurs between PV power generation and load power demand. A server should be deployed in the MGO. Scope: Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. Condition: Implementation of the ESM.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e020"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot. | Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. | The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement. | The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e005","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e021"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x001","symbol":"x_n^o","meaning":"Optimal/chosen energy consumption of prosumer n for the next time slot, submitted to the MGO.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy-consumption quantity for prosumer n in the next time slot; the cited passage does not state numerical bounds for x_n^o, while the underlying consumption decision is bounded by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max.","unit":null,"indices":["n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g01-e015"]}],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each prosumer submits its chosen next-slot energy-consumption quantity x_n^o to the MGO. Scope: Hour-ahead ESM within the microgrid; submission of each prosumer's chosen total consumption for the next time slot.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x001"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e020"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO is obligated to pursue maximization of its own profit when coordinating PV energy sharing. Scope: The MGO's objective in the Stackelberg energy-sharing arrangement.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance supplies and demands. Scope: The microgrid operator's external balancing duty under ESM. Condition: An internal mismatch occurs between PV power generation and load power demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A server should be deployed in the MGO. Scope: Infrastructure at the MGO for implementing ESM. Condition: Implementation of the ESM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e021"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. Scope: Stackelberg leader-follower coordination in the ESM arrangement.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x001"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e006"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"sumers, the effective energy sharing management (ESM) E is important for the operation. In this pape","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Moreover, an hour-ahead optimal pricing model of ESM is proposed. The model is designed based on Stackelberg game, where the MGO acts as the leader and all participating prosumers are considered as the followers. With the proof of equilibrium and uniqueness of the Stackelberg equilibrium, the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit, while the prosumers are autonomous to maximize their utilities with demand response availability."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. SYSTEM MODEL","anchor_text":", g g y he as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). i- 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV syste","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For the ESM, the involving entities can be generally divided as follows (as shown in Fig. 1). 1) PV Prosumers: The end users equipped with PV system, which can act either as supply sides or demand sides in the microgrid, determined by the profiles of load consumption and electricity generation from solar panels. When the self-produced PV energy less than the total consumption, additional energy is imported from MGO with the internal buying price p_b. Otherwise, the prosumers exports the surplus energy to MGO with the internal selling price p_s. 2) MGO: The operator of the microgrid, which conducts the optimization of energy sharing among PV prosumers. When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e020","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Each prosumer evaluates the flexible load of the next time slot, and decides the optimal energy consumption x_n^o. Every prosumer sends x_n^o to the MGO, the energy sharing of the next time slot is decided."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C Implementation Process","anchor_text":"n- set as λs and λb, respectively. 2) Every prosumer submits ˆEgn, kn, and the role of buyer or re s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to implement the ESM, a server should be deployed in the MGO, while each prosumer should be deployed with the user energy management system (U-EMS) and smart meter. The information exchanges between MGO and prosumers can be realized via advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) system [25]. As we know, this is almost the basic configuration of applications in the Smart Grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","anchor_text":"g p p mentioned studies, two main differences have been made. The as ﬁrst is the role of participant","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, every prosumer has equal privilege which means prosumers are participated in the microgrid operation equipotently. Thus, we select MGO as the leader, which means that the MGO determines the buying and selling prices simultaneously. And the prosumers act as followers to adjust their energy consumption behaviors according to the time-varying prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e015","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.A Formulation of Stackelberg Game","anchor_text":"LIU et al.: ENERGY SHARING MANAGEMENT FOR MICROGRIDS WITH PV PROSUM by changing their energy consump","equation_id":"(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The game is formally defined by its strategic form as L = {(G ∪ {MGO}), {X_n}_{n∈G}, {P_b}, {P_s}, {U_n}_{n∈G}, R} (6) which consists of the following components: 1) The prosumers in set G act as followers and choose their optimal consumption in response to the internal prices set by the MGO, the leader of the game. 2) X_n is the set of strategies of prosumer n, which is constrained by x_n^min ≤ x_n ≤ x_n^max. 3) P_b and P_s are the sets of strategies set by MGO, which are the vectors of the internal prices p_b and p_s, respectively. It should be ensured that the internal prices are constrained by λ^s ≤ p_s \u003c p_b ≤ λ^b_n. 4) U_n is the utility function of prosumer n, as shown in (1) that captures the prosumer's benefit from consuming energy x_n and sharing energy E_n^g − x_n with other prosumers in the microgrid. 5) R is the profit function of MGO, as shown in (5) that captures the total profit incurred by the sharing energy inside the microgrid and trading with the utility grid."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter is declared in this rule's frozen graph. The MGO profit objective would require p_b, p_s, E^b, E^s, λ^s, and λ^b, but those belong to pricing/clearing objects not present in this rule; importing them would violate the frozen graph, so they are requested for revision rather than declared here."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e020","quote":"Each prosumer evaluates the flexible load of the next time slot, and decides the optimal energy consumption x_n^o. Every prosumer sends x_n^o to the MGO, the energy sharing of the next time slot is decided."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e001","quote":"the MGO is obligated to coordinate the sharing of PV energy with maximization of the own profit"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","quote":"When the internal mismatch happened between power generation from PV and power demand from load, the MGO is required to trade with the utility grid to balance the supplies and demands."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e021","quote":"In order to implement the ESM, a server should be deployed in the MGO"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"1425fe754670eabb702ff87b59a7cf74ae0a6c890c98ab3f865d18f9e8ecb565","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"C001 and C004 are procedural coordination/infrastructure constraints with no supported formula. C002 and C003 have source-supported mathematical/conditional content (MGO profit maximization and utility-grid balancing), but the frozen rule graph contains only bidding.demand and coordination.local_operator with one links edge. It lacks the pricing, clearing, aggregate-quantity, and external-grid-trade objects needed to bind Eq. (5) and the mismatch condition without importing nodes from other rules. Partial supported declaration of x_n^o is retained; B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-x001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001"],"rationale":"x_n^o is the prosumer's chosen next-slot consumption quantity that the source says is sent to the MGO; it is the object carried by the frozen bidding.demand→coordination.local_operator submission relation E001."}],"revision_requests":["For C002, add source-supported pricing/clearing structure to this rule so Eq. (5) can be bound: a pricing.local decision object for p_b and p_s, a clearing.local/aggregate-quantity object for E^b and E^s, and appropriate edges to coordination.local_operator; declare p_b and p_s as MGO decision variables and λ^s and λ^b as fixed utility-grid price parameters only if C.1 adopts them for this rule.","For C003, add a graph representation of the internal mismatch condition (E^b versus E^s or equivalent PV-generation/load mismatch) and the MGO-to-utility-grid balancing action, with an edge from coordination.local_operator. The current graph cannot express the conditional external trade without inventing objects.","If C002/C003 are to be formalized, provide verified B definitions and scope for p_b, p_s, E^b, E^s, λ^s, λ^b, and the exact domain of x_n^o in this coordination rule; e020 states submission of x_n^o but no numeric bounds, and Eq. (5) belongs to the pricing/clearing stage."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
